title RecruitBook Batch 6 — Admissions Shortlists Misuse Case Slice

' Batch 6 prototype subset of the long-term MC-6
' (Unauthorized Profile Access & Consent Bypass).

actor "Verified Admissions Officer\n(misusing granted shortlist access)" as AdvAO #FFE4E6
actor "Pending / Suspended /\nUnverified Admissions Officer" as AdvUnverified #FFE4E6
actor "Malicious /\nOther Student or Counselor" as AdvStudent #FFE4E6

rectangle "Threats" {
  usecase "MC-B6-1: Keep saved-list /\ndirect-view access to a stale\n(withdrawn/unpublished/\nsuspended-owner) entry" as T1 #FFF1F2
  usecase "MC-B6-2: Infer withdrawal or\nexistence via saved-list count,\nmessage, or a distinct\nstale-entry state" as T2 #FFF1F2
  usecase "MC-B6-3: Read, save into, or\nremove ANOTHER officer's\nshortlist entry" as T3 #FFF1F2
  usecase "MC-B6-4: Forge the owner id\n(admissions_officer_application_\nuser_id) at insert" as T4 #FFF1F2
  usecase "MC-B6-5: Save a profile that is\nnot currently effectively visible\nor does not resolve to an\navailable profile (hidden,\nunpublished, consent-withdrawn,\nsuspended-owner, deleted, or\nnonexistent)" as T5 #FFF1F2
  usecase "MC-B6-6: Student or counselor\ndetects they were shortlisted\n(existence, timing, or by whom)" as T6 #FFF1F2
  usecase "MC-B6-7: Admissions write\nleaks into student_profiles,\nprofile_visibility_settings, or\ncounselor link/review/feedback\ntables" as T7 #FFF1F2
}

rectangle "Security Controls" {
  usecase "C1: is_admissions_visible_profile(\nprofile_id) evaluated at QUERY\nTIME on SELECT and INSERT" as C1 #ECFDF5
  usecase "C2: Silent omission of stale\nentries — no distinct count,\nmessage, or state; fixed generic\nsave/remove results + idempotent\nduplicate save" as C2 #ECFDF5
  usecase "C3: current_application_user_id()\nownership gate — RLS on SELECT/\nINSERT; enforced directly inside\nthe removal RPC's WHERE clause\n(not a DELETE policy)" as C3 #ECFDF5
  usecase "C4: Server-derived owner id +\ninsert ownership WITH CHECK\n(client-supplied id never trusted)" as C4 #ECFDF5
  usecase "C5: is_verified_admissions_officer()\ngate — RLS on INSERT; enforced\ninside the removal RPC (not a\nDELETE policy) (pending/suspended/\nunverified fail either way)" as C5 #ECFDF5
  usecase "C6: Deny-by-default — zero\nstudent/counselor policy on\nadmissions_shortlist_entries" as C6 #ECFDF5
  usecase "C7: No NEW admissions write\npolicy outside\nadmissions_shortlist_entries —\nexisting Batch 5 admissions\nSELECT-only access to the four\nprofile tables is UNCHANGED" as C7 #ECFDF5
}

AdvAO --> T1
AdvAO --> T2
AdvAO --> T3
AdvAO --> T4
AdvAO --> T5
AdvAO --> T7
AdvUnverified --> T3
AdvStudent --> T6

C1 ..> T1 : breaks
C1 ..> T5 : breaks
C2 ..> T2 : breaks
C3 ..> T3 : breaks
C5 ..> T3 : breaks
C4 ..> T4 : breaks
C6 ..> T6 : breaks
C7 ..> T7 : breaks

note bottom of C1
  Same live-gate-at-query-time doctrine as
  Batch 5 (is_admissions_visible_profile) and
  Batch 3/4 (is_linked_counselor_for_profile /
  is_counselor_of_live_accepted_link). No stored
  or derived visibility field on ShortlistEntry —
  a withdrawn/unpublished/suspended-owner profile
  disappears from SELECT immediately, and a
  hidden, deleted, malformed, or nonexistent
  profile id fails INSERT with the same fixed
  generic error. This is a VISIBILITY gate, not
  an ownership restriction — any verified officer
  may save any effectively visible profile,
  including one owned by another student.
end note

note bottom of C2
  No distinct "stale entry" state, count, or
  message anywhere — a hidden entry is simply
  ABSENT from the live list, never a placeholder.
  Saving an already-saved profile succeeds with
  the same fixed generic success (a unique-
  constraint violation is treated as success,
  not surfaced). Removing a foreign, stale, or
  nonexistent entry id matches zero rows and
  returns the same generic result as removing a
  real entry — no write-side oracle either.
end note

note bottom of C3
  Ownership is a direct column comparison —
  required on SELECT and INSERT under RLS, and
  re-implemented directly inside the removal
  RPC's own WHERE clause for DELETE (AMENDED:
  there is no direct DELETE RLS policy; see the
  domain-subset diagram's amendment note). Not
  merely an application-layer check either way. A
  crafted/foreign entry id belonging to another
  officer matches zero rows — under RLS for
  SELECT/INSERT, inside the RLS-bypassing
  SECURITY DEFINER RPC for removal.
end note

note right of C5
  Removal (via the hardened SECURITY DEFINER RPC
  remove_own_admissions_shortlist_entry(uuid), NOT
  a direct DELETE policy) is deliberately NOT
  visibility-gated (a documented DESIGN CHOICE,
  not a threat) — so a previously-known but now-
  stale entry remains removable by its owning
  officer. The direct-DELETE-policy proposal from
  Group 1a could not deliver this guarantee
  (Postgres ANDs SELECT-policy visibility into
  DELETE row-targeting) and was superseded by this
  RPC via a independent design-amendment review.
end note

note as N_Excluded
  Deliberately NOT modeled as threats or controls
  (out of scope for Batch 6):
  * Named or multiple shortlists; entry notes,
    labels, or tags
  * Messaging, notifications, search, ranking,
    exports, AI, uploads
  * Audit events — explicitly DEFERRED (same
    deferral as the link/review/visibility audit
    family; a future SECURITY DEFINER audit RPC
    family), not an implemented or planned
    control in this diagram
end note

note as N_Policy
  This slice is the Batch 6 prototype subset of
  the long-term MC-6 model (Unauthorized Profile
  Access & Consent Bypass) — see recruitbook_
  misuse_catalog.md Section 12. RLS is the
  database backstop; zero service-role anywhere
  in the shortlist surface. Batch 6 adds NO new
  admissions write policy anywhere outside this
  one new table. The EXISTING Batch 5 admissions
  SELECT-only access to student_profiles,
  academic_backgrounds, profile_activities, and
  profile_achievements is UNCHANGED and continues
  to apply alongside this table — it is not
  removed, narrowed, or replaced.
  profile_visibility_settings still receives no
  direct admissions policy (unchanged from Batch
  5). Counselor link/review/feedback tables still
  receive zero admissions policy (unchanged).
end note

@enduml
